5. Alternative: Lightdash-Only Stack

If you already use dbt and want a single-tool solution, Lightdash is worth evaluating:

Requirement Lightdash Fit
API-First ✅ REST API
Manual BI ✅ Visual query builder, joins, filters
AI Features ✅ Custom AI agents (BYO-key)
Exportability ✅ CSV, PNG, PDF
Self-Hosted ✅ Docker, open-source
Gap AI features are add-ons; the open-source version may have limited AI capabilities compared to Metabase.

Trade-off: Less mature than the Cube+Metabase combo; AI features may require a paid tier.

---

6. Final Recommendation

Use Cube Core + Metabase + a thin orchestration layer. This combination gives you a battle-tested semantic layer (Cube), a polished BI frontend with open-source AI features (Metabase), and just enough custom code to wire everything together. The result is a self-contained, single-tenant Docker Compose stack that satisfies all your functional and licensing constraints.

Estimated effort breakdown:

· Cube Core setup: 1–2 days
· Metabase setup: 1 day
· Orchestration layer: 5–7 days
· Integration testing: 2–3 days
· Total: ~2 weeks to a working prototype
